diff --git a/features/editing-todos.feature b/features/editing-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..10a9ba8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/editing-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+Feature: Editing todos
+  As a user
+  I want to edit existing todos
+  So that I can correct mistakes or update tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a todo activates editing mode
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks on "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is in editing mode
+    And the edit input contains "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Editing a todo and pressing Enter saves changes
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks on "Buy groceries"
+    And the user types "Buy food" in the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains "Buy food"
+    And the todo list does not contain "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Editing a todo and pressing Escape discards changes
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks on "Buy groceries"
+    And the user types "Buy food" in the edit input and presses Escape
+    Then the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo list does not contain "Buy food"
+
+  Scenario: Empty edit saves and trims input
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks on "Buy groceries"
+    And the user clears the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is removed
+
+  Scenario: Editing a todo and clicking elsewhere saves changes
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks on "Buy groceries"
+    And the user types "Buy food" in the edit input
+    And the user clicks outside the todo
+    Then the todo list contains "Buy food"
