+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+Feature: Persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos saved across page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my work
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Todos persist after page reload
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has added a completed todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo list contains "Walk the dog"
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is not completed
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is completed
+
+  Scenario: The active filter persists after page reload
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    And the page is reloaded
+    Then the "Completed" filter is selected
diff --git a/features/routing.feature b/features/routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e3e60f9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+Feature: Routing
+  As a user
+  I want to filter my todo list by status
+  So that I can focus on active or completed todos
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all todos
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has added a completed todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the user navigates to "#/"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is visible
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is visible
+    And the "All" filter is selected
+
+  Scenario: Active route shows only active todos
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has added a completed todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is visible
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is not visible
+    And the "Active" filter is selected
+
+  Scenario: Completed route shows only completed todos
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has added a completed todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is not visible
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is visible
+    And the "Completed" filter is selected
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo in active filter hides it
+    Given the user navigates to "#/active"
+    And the user has added a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user clicks the checkbox on "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is not visible
+
+  Scenario: Unchecking a todo in completed filter hides it
+    Given the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    And the user has added a completed todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user clicks the checkbox on "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is not visible
+
+  Scenario: Clearing completed while in active filter removes completed todos from model
+    Given the user has added a completed todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user has added a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    And the user clicks the Clear completed button
+    Then the todo "Walk the dog" is not visible
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is visible
diff --git a/features/toggle-all.feature b/features/toggle-all.feature
new file mode 100644
