--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/toggle-all.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+Feature: Toggle all todos
+  As a user
+  I want to mark all todos as complete at once
+  So that I can quickly complete multiple tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Clicking toggle-all marks all todos as complete
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then all todos are completed
+    And the todo count shows 0 items left
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Clicking toggle-all when all are complete marks all as active
+    Given the user has added a completed todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has added a completed todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then no todos are completed
+    And the todo count shows 2 items left
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is unchecked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all reflects the state of individual todos
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the user clicks the checkbox on "Buy groceries"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is unchecked
